1
00:00:01,914 --> 00:00:04,047
[instrumental music]

2
00:00:06,571 --> 00:00:09,444
[indistinct chattering on radio]

3
00:00:14,362 --> 00:00:15,972
[Lisbon]
'Nice place!'

4
00:00:16,059 --> 00:00:18,192
Where does a baseball scout
get this kind of money?

5
00:00:18,279 --> 00:00:19,541
Barney Sloop?

6
00:00:19,628 --> 00:00:21,108
He's got 15 players
in the majors right now

7
00:00:21,195 --> 00:00:22,805
and a piece of
everything they make.

8
00:00:22,892 --> 00:00:24,198
A million-dollar
eye for talent.

9
00:00:24,285 --> 00:00:25,547
He spots 'em young
all over the world

10
00:00:25,634 --> 00:00:27,288
brings 'em here,
trains 'em.

11
00:00:27,375 --> 00:00:28,767
Gets 'em fat pro contracts.

12
00:00:28,854 --> 00:00:32,119
Hmm. So you played.

13
00:00:32,206 --> 00:00:34,904
I played a little.

14
00:00:34,991 --> 00:00:36,036
Pitcher?

15
00:00:36,123 --> 00:00:37,689
Controlling the action?

16
00:00:37,776 --> 00:00:39,256
A man with the ball?

17
00:00:39,343 --> 00:00:41,476
Ah, I stopped.

18
00:00:41,563 --> 00:00:44,044
Which you still have
unresolved bad feelings about.

19
00:00:46,524 --> 00:00:48,918
Yeah...now I see it.

20
00:00:49,005 --> 00:00:51,268
That's why you joined the gang.

21
00:00:51,355 --> 00:00:52,965
'Parents thought you
were wasting your time'

22
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:56,056
so they made you quit
baseball, crushed your dream.

23
00:00:56,143 --> 00:00:59,276
You were angry about it, but you
couldn't express that directly

24
00:00:59,363 --> 00:01:01,974
so you joined a gang as
an outlet for all that anger.

25
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:03,802
Actually, I tore my ACL.

26
00:01:03,889 --> 00:01:05,282
- Nice try.
- Uh.

27
00:01:07,763 --> 00:01:10,592
Meh. Parents.

28
00:01:10,679 --> 00:01:12,681
It's funny, isn't it?

29
00:01:12,768 --> 00:01:15,510
Big regrets in life
people keep to themselves.

30
00:01:15,597 --> 00:01:17,686
I don't know.
I tell people about you.

31
00:01:17,773 --> 00:01:19,296
- Nice one. A zinger.
- Mm.

32
00:01:19,383 --> 00:01:20,515
High and tight.

33
00:01:21,994 --> 00:01:23,300
[male #1]
'As close as we can tell'

34
00:01:23,387 --> 00:01:26,129
'the murder occurred
around 10:30 p.m.'

35
00:01:26,216 --> 00:01:28,044
- Thanks.
- Mm-hmm.

36
00:01:28,131 --> 00:01:30,351
Eh. No big mysteries,
weapon-wise.

37
00:01:31,482 --> 00:01:32,788
Looks like three or four blows.

38
00:01:32,875 --> 00:01:34,224
Rage killing.

39
00:01:34,311 --> 00:01:35,225
[Cho]
'The coroner estimates TOD'

40
00:01:35,312 --> 00:01:37,401
'around 10:30 last night.'

41
00:01:37,488 --> 00:01:39,490
[male #2]
'You're here, finally.'

42
00:01:40,970 --> 00:01:42,798
Freddy Fitch, Barney's partner.

43
00:01:42,885 --> 00:01:44,495
I wanna know who
did this, quickly.

44
00:01:44,582 --> 00:01:48,108
Agent Lisbon.
This is Agent Cho. Jane.

45
00:01:48,195 --> 00:01:50,501
Anything you need, it's yours.

46
00:01:50,588 --> 00:01:53,069
- I can't believe it.
- This was his garden?

47
00:01:53,156 --> 00:01:55,680
His peace garden, he called it.

48
00:01:55,767 --> 00:01:58,901
A year or so ago he got
into all this Zenmalarkey.

49
00:01:58,988 --> 00:02:00,555
Who had access to this area?

50
00:02:00,642 --> 00:02:03,732
Everyone at the academy,
six players in residence

51
00:02:03,819 --> 00:02:05,734
family members, uh, staff.

52
00:02:05,821 --> 00:02:07,736
- We'll need a list.
- 'Sure, sure.'

53
00:02:07,823 --> 00:02:10,739
But trust me, n-no one
here w-w-would hurt Barney.

54
00:02:10,826 --> 00:02:12,132
You discovered the body?

55
00:02:12,219 --> 00:02:13,524
[Freddy]
'I was out of town yesterday.'

56
00:02:13,611 --> 00:02:15,004
'A high school clinic
in Portland.'

57
00:02:15,091 --> 00:02:16,440
'Flew back early this morning.'

58
00:02:16,527 --> 00:02:20,096
Came straight here,
found him like this. My God!

59
00:02:20,183 --> 00:02:24,100
[male #3]
'Run, run, run! Come on!
Work it, Scotty, work it!'

60
00:02:24,187 --> 00:02:27,451
[Lisbon]
'His body's still warm,
and they're training?'

61
00:02:27,538 --> 00:02:30,889
I said they could skip
the workout. They wouldn't.

62
00:02:30,976 --> 00:02:33,501
"Hold on to the dream."
That's what he told them.

63
00:02:35,067 --> 00:02:37,331
Barney was like
a father to these kids.

64
00:02:37,418 --> 00:02:38,897
- Pitching is legs!
- It's good, it's good..

65
00:02:38,984 --> 00:02:41,552
Look, dad, I'm ahead of you!

66
00:02:41,639 --> 00:02:43,641
Seems they have
their own fathers.

67
00:02:43,728 --> 00:02:45,948
Ah, these kids are minors.

68
00:02:46,035 --> 00:02:49,430
We bring the dads out to sign
off on deals, moral support.

69
00:02:52,041 --> 00:02:55,349
'Scotty Sinclair
and Snake Gallidos.'

70
00:02:55,436 --> 00:02:57,786
Five drooling
scouts coming today.

71
00:02:57,873 --> 00:03:00,092
Maybe now isn't
the best time.

72
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:03,183
Barney set this up,
his last showcase.

73
00:03:04,358 --> 00:03:05,533
I'm gonna honor that.

74
00:03:05,620 --> 00:03:08,362
'It's what Barney would want.'

75
00:03:08,449 --> 00:03:12,148
I know you gotta talk to them.
It's your job, but please..

76
00:03:12,235 --> 00:03:13,889
Hey, we can let the kids
finish their practice.

77
00:03:13,976 --> 00:03:14,933
Let's take a look at his house.

78
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:16,413
How do you know where it's at?

79
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:20,200
'Cause this thing is
a map of his whole life.

80
00:03:21,113 --> 00:03:23,986
Work, garden, home.

81
00:03:25,030 --> 00:03:26,162
Zenmalarkey.

82
00:03:27,555 --> 00:03:29,513
[indistinct chattering]

83
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:32,473
I don't expect it's much to look
at, a simple bed or a thing or..

84
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:33,517
Oh!

85
00:03:36,390 --> 00:03:39,219
[theme music]

86
00:03:46,835 --> 00:03:49,664
Jane? Jane?

87
00:03:49,751 --> 00:03:51,318
Hey, you alright?

88
00:03:51,405 --> 00:03:53,276
- 'Jane?'
- I see it.

89
00:03:55,539 --> 00:03:59,282
- 'Cigarette case.'
- 'A cigarette case. Yes!'

90
00:03:59,369 --> 00:04:01,676
Yes! Very good.

91
00:04:01,763 --> 00:04:03,678
But..

92
00:04:03,765 --> 00:04:06,115
'...what's it made of, son?'

93
00:04:06,202 --> 00:04:09,771
What kind of
cigarette case, Patrick?

94
00:04:11,686 --> 00:04:13,340
'What would you say?'

95
00:04:13,427 --> 00:04:16,081
What's it made of?

96
00:04:16,168 --> 00:04:18,214
[chuckles]
Sterling silver.

97
00:04:19,433 --> 00:04:22,174
[laughing]

98
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:27,092
Your sterling silver
cigarette case back, ma'am.

99
00:04:27,179 --> 00:04:29,573
- Next object would be--
- The cigarette case.

100
00:04:32,228 --> 00:04:35,666
It once belonged to someone
very, very close to you.

101
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:38,887
That's right.

102
00:04:38,974 --> 00:04:42,369
Yes. The boy wonder sees all.

103
00:04:42,456 --> 00:04:44,806
'The next object, Patrick.'

104
00:04:44,893 --> 00:04:48,113
Someone who's passed on..

105
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:51,203
...quite recently.

106
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:52,814
Last month.

107
00:04:52,901 --> 00:04:54,859
Your grandfather.

108
00:04:54,946 --> 00:04:56,948
No.

109
00:04:57,035 --> 00:04:58,602
Your grandmother.

110
00:05:01,257 --> 00:05:03,520
She loves you.

111
00:05:03,607 --> 00:05:06,306
Very much.

112
00:05:06,393 --> 00:05:08,351
More than she
may have expressed.

113
00:05:12,137 --> 00:05:13,748
What the hell was that?

114
00:05:13,835 --> 00:05:16,011
Your grandmother
loves you very much?

115
00:05:16,098 --> 00:05:18,361
Well, did you see her face?

116
00:05:18,448 --> 00:05:21,843
- It was beautiful.
- No. It was a needless risk.

117
00:05:21,930 --> 00:05:23,758
An heirloom she
carries with her.

118
00:05:23,845 --> 00:05:25,150
That's a recent death.

119
00:05:25,237 --> 00:05:27,327
And she's too young
for dead parents.

120
00:05:27,414 --> 00:05:31,548
- So a grandparent.
- So what? I'd moved on.

121
00:05:31,635 --> 00:05:33,376
It's a double act, kid.

122
00:05:33,463 --> 00:05:34,986
You don't fly solo.

123
00:05:35,073 --> 00:05:36,553
Now you're always saying,
"when you're working strong

124
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:37,989
work strong, be brave."

125
00:05:38,076 --> 00:05:40,818
Well, I was working
strong, and I was right.

126
00:05:40,905 --> 00:05:45,562
No...there is no right
if there's no payoff.

127
00:05:45,649 --> 00:05:47,912
This is show business,
not show art.

128
00:05:51,916 --> 00:05:54,571
Your stage clothes are
walking by themselves.

129
00:05:54,658 --> 00:05:56,181
Wash 'em good.

130
00:05:56,268 --> 00:05:59,184
[indistinct chattering]

131
00:06:01,883 --> 00:06:03,275
Hey!

132
00:06:04,929 --> 00:06:06,844
That private reading..

133
00:06:10,457 --> 00:06:12,850
...it came through.

134
00:06:12,937 --> 00:06:15,723
- You got it? When?
- Tomorrow.

135
00:06:15,810 --> 00:06:17,551
This is a big score, Patty.

136
00:06:17,638 --> 00:06:19,770
Big enough for us to
blow off this outfit

137
00:06:19,857 --> 00:06:21,206
step up in class

138
00:06:21,293 --> 00:06:24,166
and get ourselves
some new wheels even.

139
00:06:25,950 --> 00:06:27,865
Only one thing worries me.

140
00:06:30,912 --> 00:06:32,740
It's you, myboy.

141
00:06:32,827 --> 00:06:34,306
You up to it?

142
00:06:34,394 --> 00:06:36,091
Oh, you know I am.

143
00:06:38,485 --> 00:06:40,791
Of course, you are.

144
00:06:40,878 --> 00:06:42,837
The boy wonder sees all.

145
00:06:47,494 --> 00:06:49,191
Can you stand up?

146
00:06:52,803 --> 00:06:55,937
- Can you talk?
- Ouch.

147
00:06:56,024 --> 00:06:57,591
I was talking.

148
00:06:57,678 --> 00:07:00,463
- He needs to see a doctor.
- Yeah.

149
00:07:00,550 --> 00:07:04,119
Wow. I've never caught
a foul ball before.

150
00:07:04,206 --> 00:07:06,208
Technically, you still haven't.

151
00:07:06,295 --> 00:07:07,601
- Cho, you take him.
- Yeah.

152
00:07:07,688 --> 00:07:09,646
Oh, no, no, no. I'm fine.

153
00:07:09,733 --> 00:07:10,952
- How many fingers?
- Six.

154
00:07:11,039 --> 00:07:12,301
Haven't we got
a murder to solve?

155
00:07:12,388 --> 00:07:13,824
- You were unconscious.
- No, I wasn't.

156
00:07:13,911 --> 00:07:16,479
- Jane, you were.
- I was not.

157
00:07:16,566 --> 00:07:20,222
Your turn.
Okay, I'll see a doctor.

158
00:07:20,309 --> 00:07:22,746
- Uh, excuse me, doctor?
- Hmm?

159
00:07:24,748 --> 00:07:27,316
I know. Real-life patient.
I'm excited too.

160
00:07:29,623 --> 00:07:33,583
Barney lived simple.
All work, all the time, 24/7.

161
00:07:33,670 --> 00:07:36,281
Left his wife,
gave her the big house.

162
00:07:36,368 --> 00:07:39,589
A clean, simple life
that's all he wanted.

163
00:07:39,676 --> 00:07:41,286
- Barney was married?
- 'Still is.'

164
00:07:41,373 --> 00:07:42,766
[Freddy]
'Leslie, a piece of work.'

165
00:07:42,853 --> 00:07:44,986
'Like I said, he
moved out a year ago.'

166
00:07:46,422 --> 00:07:48,380
After their son died.

167
00:07:51,558 --> 00:07:53,734
He was three.
Choked on a balloon.

168
00:07:53,821 --> 00:07:56,388
'Leslie just fell apart.'

169
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:59,653
'Angry at Barney, the whole
world, couldn't get past it.'

170
00:07:59,740 --> 00:08:02,569
I called her this morning
after I called you.

171
00:08:02,656 --> 00:08:04,875
She wouldn't even
pick up the phone.

172
00:08:04,962 --> 00:08:10,141
The way I see it...bad things
happen, and you deal with 'em.

173
00:08:10,228 --> 00:08:11,752
And Barney did?

174
00:08:11,839 --> 00:08:14,624
Uh, he put his head
down, went to work.

175
00:08:14,711 --> 00:08:19,194
Found Snake in the Dominican and
Scotty somewhere in-in Kansas.

176
00:08:19,281 --> 00:08:24,504
Meanwhile, Leslie is...stuck
living in a, in a world of hurt.

177
00:08:25,896 --> 00:08:29,509
Hmm. I feel it.

178
00:08:30,945 --> 00:08:33,208
Let's check
the wife, Leslie Sloop.

179
00:08:34,165 --> 00:08:36,080
[keyboard keys clacking]

180
00:08:38,082 --> 00:08:40,911
- Working.
- Okay.

181
00:08:46,351 --> 00:08:48,353
Drinking like a fish..

182
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:50,530
...picking up strangers..

183
00:08:50,617 --> 00:08:52,880
...callin' Barney at all hours..

184
00:08:52,967 --> 00:08:54,359
...screamin'.

185
00:08:54,446 --> 00:08:57,188
I don't get that
kind of anger.

186
00:08:57,275 --> 00:08:59,321
Okay, her kid died.

187
00:08:59,408 --> 00:09:01,149
Is-is that gonna bring him back?

188
00:09:01,236 --> 00:09:03,368
You don't have kids.

189
00:09:03,455 --> 00:09:05,066
No, I don't.

190
00:09:05,153 --> 00:09:07,372
'Uh, the ballplayers
should be heading in.'

191
00:09:08,722 --> 00:09:09,897
With Barney dead,
I'm assuming

192
00:09:09,984 --> 00:09:11,072
that you get the, uh

193
00:09:11,159 --> 00:09:13,727
controlling interest
in the academy.

194
00:09:13,814 --> 00:09:15,990
- What's that got to do with it?
- Money.

195
00:09:16,077 --> 00:09:17,992
Traditionally a very
popular motive.

196
00:09:18,732 --> 00:09:20,124
Excuse me?

197
00:09:20,211 --> 00:09:21,430
I imagine these two
had their differences

198
00:09:21,517 --> 00:09:22,953
'the gold watch,
the Italian suit.'

199
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:24,302
Oh, I'm sorry,
the Taiwanese suit

200
00:09:24,389 --> 00:09:25,739
made to look Italian.

201
00:09:27,392 --> 00:09:28,785
I don't have to listen to this.

202
00:09:28,872 --> 00:09:31,266
Not exactly emblems of
the clean, simple life.

203
00:09:31,353 --> 00:09:32,310
There was a culture clash, yeah?

204
00:09:32,397 --> 00:09:33,747
- No.
- Jane.

205
00:09:33,834 --> 00:09:35,357
Plus, what is it exactly

206
00:09:35,444 --> 00:09:37,011
you bring to the table?

207
00:09:37,098 --> 00:09:39,535
Barney was the brains,
the real scout, the star.

208
00:09:39,622 --> 00:09:41,537
I mean, the Sloop Academy.

209
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:46,194
Jealousy, motive number two.

210
00:09:46,281 --> 00:09:48,283
I killed him.
I-I murdered my best friend.

211
00:09:48,370 --> 00:09:49,589
- Did you?
- Jane, come on.

212
00:09:49,676 --> 00:09:50,938
Get this jerk away from me.

213
00:09:51,025 --> 00:09:52,548
Seriously, get it
off your chest.

214
00:09:52,635 --> 00:09:54,855
- You'll feel a lot better.
- He was my friend!

215
00:09:54,942 --> 00:09:57,248
How did that feel, crushing your
friend's skull with that bat?

216
00:09:57,335 --> 00:10:00,121
- How did that feel?
- Hey, hey, hey.

217
00:10:00,208 --> 00:10:02,166
- Back off now.
- I'm just checking him out.

218
00:10:02,253 --> 00:10:03,820
And?

219
00:10:03,907 --> 00:10:06,910
Well, ambivalent
reading, to be honest.

220
00:10:06,997 --> 00:10:08,782
'Maybe he did it.
Maybe he didn't.'

221
00:10:08,869 --> 00:10:11,088
But one thing he does
understand, that's anger.

222
00:10:13,743 --> 00:10:16,441
No offense.

223
00:10:16,528 --> 00:10:18,443
[Freddy]
None taken, jerk.

224
00:10:20,445 --> 00:10:22,796
[sighs]
You think I can
skip these interviews?

225
00:10:22,883 --> 00:10:24,798
- Please.
- Thanks.

226
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:34,155
[Lisbon]
'Scotty Sinclair?'

227
00:10:35,504 --> 00:10:37,419
Doc Sinclair. He's 17.

228
00:10:37,506 --> 00:10:39,421
You're talkin' to him,
you're talkin' to me.

229
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:45,993
[instrumental music]

230
00:10:53,870 --> 00:10:56,830
[Snake]
'Two, maybe three months ago..'

231
00:10:56,917 --> 00:11:01,138
...I was having control
trouble, my slider.

232
00:11:01,225 --> 00:11:03,880
Mr. Sloop said I
needed to quiet my brain.

233
00:11:05,752 --> 00:11:08,232
We raked together in his garden.

234
00:11:08,319 --> 00:11:09,277
It worked.

235
00:11:13,411 --> 00:11:15,631
I would never hurt Mr. Sloop.

236
00:11:15,718 --> 00:11:18,590
He gave me everything.
He brought me here.

237
00:11:18,678 --> 00:11:22,507
He hooked me up with great
coaches, regular school.

238
00:11:22,594 --> 00:11:24,596
And money to live on?

239
00:11:24,684 --> 00:11:27,687
An advance, some kind
of endorsement deal?

240
00:11:27,774 --> 00:11:29,471
Got, like, ten free pairs.

241
00:11:32,169 --> 00:11:35,085
Which we're gonna have to pay
back if he blows this showcase.

242
00:11:35,172 --> 00:11:38,349
Barney cared. Okay?

243
00:11:38,436 --> 00:11:41,135
He taught us how to
handle money, invest it.

244
00:11:42,614 --> 00:11:44,355
He taught us how to handle life.

245
00:11:44,442 --> 00:11:46,880
Are we done yet?

246
00:11:46,967 --> 00:11:49,317
He's supposed to be
throwing right now.

247
00:11:49,404 --> 00:11:52,059
Right, yeah.
Got it. Thanks, Frank.

248
00:11:53,538 --> 00:11:55,105
Whew!

249
00:11:55,192 --> 00:11:58,282
Barney's life insurance payout,
twenty million dollars.

250
00:11:58,369 --> 00:12:01,503
Let me guess, sole
beneficiary Leslie Sloop.

251
00:12:01,590 --> 00:12:03,940
Twenty million.
That's a pretty good motive.

252
00:12:04,027 --> 00:12:07,117
For twenty million dollars
I'd kill you.

253
00:12:07,204 --> 00:12:10,468
- Oh, really?
- No, I mean, I'm kidding.

254
00:12:10,555 --> 00:12:12,644
- It was a joke.
- Huh.

255
00:12:15,038 --> 00:12:17,388
- Still the machine.
- Let's go see her.

256
00:12:22,219 --> 00:12:24,091
Someone needs parking lessons.

257
00:12:27,921 --> 00:12:29,096
Who are you?

258
00:12:29,183 --> 00:12:31,141
We're looking for Leslie Sloop.

259
00:12:31,228 --> 00:12:34,449
Bitch ain't here, man,
and I called the real cops.

260
00:12:34,536 --> 00:12:37,104
- Hey, man, what took you?
- Hey, Narcisco!

261
00:12:37,191 --> 00:12:39,149
- Wait. You know him?
- You don't?

262
00:12:39,236 --> 00:12:41,761
Narcisco Rubrero.

263
00:12:41,848 --> 00:12:43,588
Walk-off homer,
game one, world series?

264
00:12:43,675 --> 00:12:44,981
Huh. Well.

265
00:12:45,068 --> 00:12:47,027
Help us out, Narcisco.
Where is she?

266
00:12:47,114 --> 00:12:48,724
Let's go downtown
and get a statement.

267
00:12:48,811 --> 00:12:50,552
- 'Alright.'
- Hold on, you guys.

268
00:12:50,639 --> 00:12:52,772
- We got dibs here.
- She scratched my face.

269
00:12:53,990 --> 00:12:55,775
I think I'm bleedin'.

270
00:12:55,862 --> 00:12:58,560
Look, she smashes her car,
so she steals mine.

271
00:12:58,647 --> 00:13:00,605
- My Lamborghini.
- Where did she go?

272
00:13:02,912 --> 00:13:05,480
I got a gun in that car.
It's all legal.

273
00:13:05,567 --> 00:13:07,395
I got, like a,
got like a permit.

274
00:13:07,482 --> 00:13:09,876
- Narcisco, where is she?
- I don't know, man.

275
00:13:09,963 --> 00:13:11,878
She kept screaming
about her little angel.

276
00:13:11,965 --> 00:13:14,445
You know, she had to
see her little angel.

277
00:13:14,532 --> 00:13:15,969
The son, Michael.

278
00:13:18,014 --> 00:13:20,538
Hey. Hey! She stole my car!

279
00:13:20,625 --> 00:13:22,497
So take it up
with the real cops.

280
00:13:27,197 --> 00:13:29,634
Jane, Lisbon wants
us back at the office.

281
00:13:38,730 --> 00:13:41,472
Jane, wrong way.

282
00:13:41,559 --> 00:13:43,344
Jane!

283
00:13:43,431 --> 00:13:46,303
[instrumental music]

284
00:13:57,532 --> 00:13:58,838
What are you doing?

285
00:14:00,796 --> 00:14:03,712
[rustling]

286
00:14:03,799 --> 00:14:06,715
[music continues]

287
00:14:12,155 --> 00:14:14,679
They say there's no
seasons in California

288
00:14:14,766 --> 00:14:16,768
but that looks like fall.

289
00:14:19,946 --> 00:14:22,035
No, looks like
you need a doctor.

290
00:14:22,122 --> 00:14:23,558
I am kind of dizzy.

291
00:14:28,563 --> 00:14:31,435
[clapping]

292
00:14:31,522 --> 00:14:32,654
[male #4]
'One more time.'

293
00:14:32,741 --> 00:14:35,048
[clanging]

294
00:14:36,310 --> 00:14:39,400
[male #5]
'Okay, hotshot.'

295
00:14:39,487 --> 00:14:42,403
'Female, third in line.'

296
00:14:42,490 --> 00:14:43,404
[Jane]
'Okay.'

297
00:14:45,841 --> 00:14:49,889
New mom, recently married.
One of her first days out.

298
00:14:53,196 --> 00:14:55,372
He is gonna get
her a better ring.

299
00:14:55,459 --> 00:14:57,766
- Who is?
- Members only.

300
00:15:00,334 --> 00:15:02,597
[indistinct chattering]

301
00:15:02,684 --> 00:15:04,425
[Jane]
'They hadto get married.'

302
00:15:04,512 --> 00:15:06,166
[laughs]

303
00:15:07,471 --> 00:15:09,256
Yeah, that's my boy.

304
00:15:10,605 --> 00:15:13,434
You have x-ray eyes.
No doubt about it.

305
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:21,311
Whew!

306
00:15:21,398 --> 00:15:25,011
- Jane?
- Hey.

307
00:15:26,316 --> 00:15:27,622
I'm okay.

308
00:15:31,495 --> 00:15:32,932
Whew!

309
00:15:36,152 --> 00:15:39,503
Snake and Scotty are about
to pitch. We can't miss that.

310
00:15:39,590 --> 00:15:43,507
Oh, Michael, I'm so sorry.
What did I do?

311
00:15:48,034 --> 00:15:48,991
[sobbing]

312
00:15:50,906 --> 00:15:52,038
Mrs. Sloop?

313
00:15:53,865 --> 00:15:55,476
I'm with my son.

314
00:15:57,260 --> 00:15:59,349
Mrs. Sloop, I'm sorry,
we need to talk to you

315
00:15:59,436 --> 00:16:00,742
about your husband.

316
00:16:00,829 --> 00:16:02,831
No, no. You need to go.

317
00:16:04,050 --> 00:16:05,616
Really, you do.

318
00:16:08,228 --> 00:16:10,230
Don't you see this is private?

319
00:16:13,581 --> 00:16:15,104
[dramatic music]

320
00:16:20,022 --> 00:16:21,284
I don't want to talk.

321
00:16:21,371 --> 00:16:26,246
I just...I just,
I want to end this.

322
00:16:26,333 --> 00:16:30,250
- Please, just leave me alone.
- I'm sorry. We can't do that.

323
00:16:30,337 --> 00:16:32,078
You have to. Please.

324
00:16:34,645 --> 00:16:39,476
Because I...I don't
know what else to do.

325
00:16:40,390 --> 00:16:41,783
Mrs. Sloop.

326
00:16:41,870 --> 00:16:43,872
Oh, my God. I'm so sorry.

327
00:16:43,959 --> 00:16:46,222
I've never had children.

328
00:16:46,309 --> 00:16:48,572
I-I can't even begin
to imagine your loss.

329
00:16:48,659 --> 00:16:50,922
No. No, you can't.
So just stop.

330
00:16:53,621 --> 00:16:55,753
Please, just leave me alone.

331
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:57,799
'Just stop talking.'

332
00:17:00,410 --> 00:17:02,804
I'm not going to stop. I can't.

333
00:17:05,763 --> 00:17:08,244
My sister, she
was just like you.

334
00:17:08,331 --> 00:17:10,855
I don't, I don't
want to hear this.

335
00:17:10,942 --> 00:17:14,598
She wanted it to
beover...for her.

336
00:17:17,166 --> 00:17:19,516
It was always about her.

337
00:17:19,603 --> 00:17:21,475
'She couldn't talk to me.'

338
00:17:21,562 --> 00:17:24,869
- About what?
- About anything.

339
00:17:24,956 --> 00:17:28,395
I'm her sister.
But she didn't.

340
00:17:28,482 --> 00:17:30,397
Not to me, not to anybody.

341
00:17:32,747 --> 00:17:35,097
She just ended it for her.

342
00:17:36,533 --> 00:17:38,535
I don't know what else to do.

343
00:17:41,495 --> 00:17:43,062
Give me the gun.

344
00:17:46,587 --> 00:17:47,936
Put it down.

345
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:52,027
You don't wanna
do this. Not here.

346
00:17:52,114 --> 00:17:53,594
Give me the gun.

347
00:17:57,511 --> 00:17:59,382
[sobbing]
I'm so sorry, Michael.

348
00:17:59,469 --> 00:18:01,819
[Rigsby]
'It's okay.
Come on. It's okay.'

349
00:18:03,647 --> 00:18:06,128
[indistinct chattering]

350
00:18:07,303 --> 00:18:08,870
Not now. You know that.

351
00:18:10,393 --> 00:18:11,742
'Okay. Okay.'

352
00:18:13,527 --> 00:18:16,617
Look, I'm busy here.
Your brother's tryout is today.

353
00:18:18,227 --> 00:18:20,011
'No. No way.'

354
00:18:22,579 --> 00:18:23,798
Bye.

355
00:18:23,885 --> 00:18:26,540
[indistinct chattering]

356
00:18:27,976 --> 00:18:31,110
- Hey.
- That's my older boy.

357
00:18:31,197 --> 00:18:34,504
He's a pitcher,
just like Snake.

358
00:18:34,591 --> 00:18:36,419
He's just as good too.

359
00:18:36,506 --> 00:18:38,378
But he's 22.

360
00:18:38,465 --> 00:18:41,424
In baseball years,
he's an old man.

361
00:18:41,511 --> 00:18:43,600
Yeah, these pro teams, they
like 'em young these days.

362
00:18:43,687 --> 00:18:45,689
Like Snake.

363
00:18:45,776 --> 00:18:47,648
Plenty of time for improvement.

364
00:18:49,911 --> 00:18:52,870
[indistinct chattering]

365
00:18:52,957 --> 00:18:54,698
We caught a break.
The wife looks good for it.

366
00:18:58,049 --> 00:19:00,095
What was that? Was that a fork?

367
00:19:00,182 --> 00:19:02,880
- Did he just throw a forkball?
- It was a slider.

368
00:19:02,967 --> 00:19:04,578
We gotta go. Lisbon wants you
to take a look at the wife.

369
00:19:04,665 --> 00:19:07,581
"Slider?" You know,
I'm still a little dizzy.

370
00:19:09,322 --> 00:19:12,716
You go. Really,
I-I, I'll get a ride.

371
00:19:12,803 --> 00:19:14,675
People love
driving with me.

372
00:19:17,765 --> 00:19:20,246
Couldn't find sunflowers.

373
00:19:20,333 --> 00:19:23,031
'Not quite the same.'

374
00:19:23,118 --> 00:19:25,338
[Lisbon]
'Leslie, where
were you last night?'

375
00:19:25,425 --> 00:19:26,861
[Leslie]
'We went to the movies.'

376
00:19:26,948 --> 00:19:31,300
I don't...I don't
remember which one.

377
00:19:31,387 --> 00:19:33,259
You're not supposed to take
these when you're drinking.

378
00:19:33,346 --> 00:19:34,999
It was so loud.

379
00:19:35,086 --> 00:19:37,480
There were guns
and helicopters

380
00:19:37,567 --> 00:19:39,047
and people screaming.

381
00:19:39,134 --> 00:19:42,268
Ugh, there was
so much screaming.

382
00:19:42,355 --> 00:19:44,487
Darn. These are
supposed to keep me calm.

383
00:19:44,574 --> 00:19:47,403
[chuckles]
Just one a day.

384
00:19:47,490 --> 00:19:49,362
That's what the doctor said.
That'll do the trick.

385
00:19:49,449 --> 00:19:51,581
Leslie, did you go
and see Barney last night?

386
00:19:51,668 --> 00:19:53,540
To see Barney?

387
00:19:54,889 --> 00:19:58,893
Mr. Zen?Mr. Acceptance?

388
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:00,155
[scoffs]

389
00:20:01,069 --> 00:20:02,984
Why would I do that?

390
00:20:05,595 --> 00:20:08,250
- 'Tell us about Narcisco.'
- Narcisco?

391
00:20:10,470 --> 00:20:11,906
Oh, yeah.

392
00:20:11,993 --> 00:20:13,951
[chuckles]

393
00:20:14,038 --> 00:20:16,432
He's one of Barney's players.

394
00:20:16,519 --> 00:20:18,695
'I sometimes slept
with those guys.'

395
00:20:18,782 --> 00:20:20,175
'Did you know that?'

396
00:20:20,262 --> 00:20:23,700
I did that sometimes...
to make him mad.

397
00:20:25,963 --> 00:20:28,139
He didn't even care.

398
00:20:30,011 --> 00:20:31,752
She's going around and around.

399
00:20:31,839 --> 00:20:34,972
But I think she's
gonna give it up.

400
00:20:35,059 --> 00:20:38,106
I thought you were, uh,
amazing out there today.

401
00:20:38,193 --> 00:20:40,239
I just, just wanted
to tell you that.

402
00:20:41,849 --> 00:20:44,678
Thank you, I guess.

403
00:20:44,765 --> 00:20:48,595
- Can I ask you something?
- I don't have a sister.

404
00:20:48,682 --> 00:20:49,857
No.

405
00:20:49,944 --> 00:20:51,946
I didn't remember one.

406
00:20:52,033 --> 00:20:54,427
It just...came out.

407
00:20:57,038 --> 00:20:59,432
[indistinct chattering]

408
00:20:59,519 --> 00:21:00,433
Come on.

409
00:21:02,870 --> 00:21:05,525
[indistinct chattering]

410
00:21:06,482 --> 00:21:07,396
Come on. Come on!

411
00:21:08,571 --> 00:21:11,270
Ah! What was that?

412
00:21:12,793 --> 00:21:15,361
Come on, Scotty!
What are you thinkin'?

413
00:21:15,448 --> 00:21:17,885
- 'Come on!'
- He gets down on him too much.

414
00:21:19,495 --> 00:21:22,542
- The boy can throw.
- Mmm. He can hit too.

415
00:21:22,629 --> 00:21:25,066
Last night in the cage,
he dinged me three times

416
00:21:25,153 --> 00:21:26,241
'off my slider.'

417
00:21:26,328 --> 00:21:28,025
Nobody touches my slider.

418
00:21:28,112 --> 00:21:30,027
That man is gonna
kill the golden goose.

419
00:21:30,114 --> 00:21:31,377
Scotty plays like this now.

420
00:21:31,464 --> 00:21:34,728
Imagine when he's
18 or 20 years old.

421
00:21:34,815 --> 00:21:36,947
He's only gonna get better.

422
00:21:37,034 --> 00:21:38,645
'It's amazing, huh?'

423
00:21:40,734 --> 00:21:42,997
[alarm blaring]

424
00:21:43,084 --> 00:21:46,000
[indistinct chattering]

425
00:21:47,567 --> 00:21:50,265
[carnival music]

426
00:21:54,574 --> 00:21:56,837
Ah! There.

427
00:21:57,751 --> 00:21:58,839
Hmm.

428
00:22:00,710 --> 00:22:05,106
'I spent three long days
at that crummy hospital'

429
00:22:05,193 --> 00:22:08,849
finding the mark...
setting up the play.

430
00:22:10,198 --> 00:22:12,287
And now..

431
00:22:12,374 --> 00:22:14,507
...it's time to get paid.

432
00:22:14,594 --> 00:22:17,423
[intense music]

433
00:22:25,996 --> 00:22:28,912
[whirring]

434
00:22:32,046 --> 00:22:34,918
[instrumental music]

435
00:22:37,312 --> 00:22:39,706
[whirring continues]

436
00:22:40,707 --> 00:22:41,621
[whirring stops]

437
00:22:42,970 --> 00:22:46,060
Hey! We've been waiting for you.

438
00:22:46,147 --> 00:22:49,933
- How you doing?
- Whoo! Go, Cho!

439
00:22:50,020 --> 00:22:52,283
Hey! CBI! Stop!

440
00:22:52,371 --> 00:22:55,374
Hey! Get back here! Hey!

441
00:22:55,461 --> 00:22:58,377
[whirring continues]

442
00:23:06,254 --> 00:23:09,126
[whirring continues]

443
00:23:15,045 --> 00:23:17,308
[instrumental music]

444
00:23:17,396 --> 00:23:20,050
[Lisbon]
'Leslie, we talked to
five bars near the beach.'

445
00:23:21,095 --> 00:23:22,183
Nothing.

446
00:23:26,405 --> 00:23:29,364
After the movies, I had
an argument with Narcisco

447
00:23:29,451 --> 00:23:31,018
and went to Barney's.

448
00:23:31,105 --> 00:23:32,715
[crying]

449
00:23:32,802 --> 00:23:37,154
He was sleeping...
in his garden.

450
00:23:37,241 --> 00:23:39,722
- He wouldn't even talk to me.
- Leslie.

451
00:23:39,809 --> 00:23:42,290
I'm his wife.

452
00:23:42,377 --> 00:23:45,075
I'm the mother of his child.
Shouldn't he talk to me?

453
00:23:53,214 --> 00:23:55,564
She was there that night,
but he was already dead?

454
00:23:55,651 --> 00:23:57,305
If they were at
a 10 o'clock movie, it adds up.

455
00:23:57,392 --> 00:23:58,480
She knew he was dead.

456
00:23:58,567 --> 00:24:01,004
That's what pushed
her over the edge.

457
00:24:01,091 --> 00:24:03,398
I didn't, I didn't kill him.

458
00:24:03,485 --> 00:24:06,270
I couldn't, even if I wanted to.

459
00:24:06,357 --> 00:24:08,055
What would I tell Michael?

460
00:24:10,187 --> 00:24:12,059
Mmm, you should let her go.

461
00:24:12,146 --> 00:24:14,714
Where? Even if she didn't
kill him, she needs help.

462
00:24:17,194 --> 00:24:18,544
Your pants are ripped.

463
00:24:18,631 --> 00:24:21,677
We found a witness
with immigration problems.

464
00:24:21,764 --> 00:24:24,593
A baseball player, he was
very angry with Mr. Sloop.

465
00:24:24,680 --> 00:24:27,988
- Yesterday afternoon?
- He was yelling. Loud.

466
00:24:28,075 --> 00:24:29,816
He say Mr. Sloop
was stealing.

467
00:24:29,903 --> 00:24:31,992
And Mr. Sloop,
he was very quiet.

468
00:24:32,079 --> 00:24:34,255
He was trying to walk away,
but the baseball player

469
00:24:34,342 --> 00:24:35,909
he followed him, very angry.

470
00:24:35,996 --> 00:24:37,432
That's it?

471
00:24:39,913 --> 00:24:42,393
Um, Mr. Sloop, he
went into his trailer.

472
00:24:42,481 --> 00:24:44,047
Then he come out
and he show him some papers.

473
00:24:44,134 --> 00:24:46,615
And then the baseball
player, he got quiet.

474
00:24:46,702 --> 00:24:48,095
And that's when I left.

475
00:24:48,182 --> 00:24:49,531
But he'd recognize
the player if he saw him again.

476
00:24:52,099 --> 00:24:54,014
- Yes.
- Mmm.

477
00:24:57,539 --> 00:24:59,759
[male #6]
'Alright, line up
facing the mirror.'

478
00:25:04,764 --> 00:25:06,766
It's the biggest day of their
lives. Don't you get that?

479
00:25:06,853 --> 00:25:09,769
Barney Sloop had his head
bashed in, Mr. Gallidos.

480
00:25:09,856 --> 00:25:11,553
Big day for him too.

481
00:25:15,165 --> 00:25:18,038
[instrumental music]

482
00:25:24,566 --> 00:25:26,873
[music continues]

483
00:25:28,744 --> 00:25:31,355
- Him.
- You sure?

484
00:25:31,442 --> 00:25:33,923
Him at the end.

485
00:25:34,010 --> 00:25:35,534
[male #3]
'It's just not true.'

486
00:25:35,621 --> 00:25:37,666
- Dad--
- Hey! I've got this!

487
00:25:40,843 --> 00:25:42,062
My boy doesn't lie.

488
00:25:42,149 --> 00:25:44,020
- If he said he didn't--
- I did.

489
00:25:46,196 --> 00:25:49,373
I went to see him, alright?
But, I mean, I didn't kill him.

490
00:25:49,460 --> 00:25:52,638
- What were you arguing about?
- I don't believe it.

491
00:25:52,725 --> 00:25:54,770
- You lied to me?
- Mr. Sinclair, please.

492
00:25:54,857 --> 00:25:57,338
Yeah. I'm sorry
to disappoint you, dad.

493
00:25:59,514 --> 00:26:02,430
What were you arguing about?
What did Barney steal?

494
00:26:02,517 --> 00:26:05,389
He's not saying one word
because we're leaving now.

495
00:26:05,476 --> 00:26:06,434
Mr. Fitch--

496
00:26:06,521 --> 00:26:07,522
Scotty had an argument

497
00:26:07,609 --> 00:26:09,524
with Barney hours before

498
00:26:09,611 --> 00:26:10,786
the murder.

499
00:26:10,873 --> 00:26:12,919
You got nothing to hold him on.

500
00:26:13,006 --> 00:26:14,485
Not yet.

501
00:26:16,792 --> 00:26:19,665
[instrumental music]

502
00:26:24,408 --> 00:26:26,933
[Lisbon]
'He had an argument with
Barney. He was angry.'

503
00:26:27,020 --> 00:26:28,717
He lied about it.

504
00:26:28,804 --> 00:26:30,719
Who's to say Scotty
didn't go back that night

505
00:26:30,806 --> 00:26:31,764
and kill the guy?

506
00:26:31,851 --> 00:26:33,243
The kid didn't do it.

507
00:26:33,330 --> 00:26:35,376
He was angry with his
dad, not with Sloop.

508
00:26:35,463 --> 00:26:38,161
If you think he did it,
then check the cameras.

509
00:26:38,248 --> 00:26:39,554
What camera?

510
00:26:39,641 --> 00:26:42,078
The baseball field cameras.

511
00:26:42,165 --> 00:26:43,471
Snake let slip
that he and Scotty

512
00:26:43,558 --> 00:26:44,515
were out there last night.

513
00:26:44,603 --> 00:26:46,082
Apparently, Scotty handled

514
00:26:46,169 --> 00:26:47,867
Snake's slider very well.

515
00:26:49,869 --> 00:26:52,523
- You sure you're alright?
- Yeah. I'm fine.

516
00:26:52,611 --> 00:26:54,264
Security cam.

517
00:26:54,351 --> 00:26:57,093
Should be time-stamped.

518
00:26:57,180 --> 00:26:59,618
[Grace]
'The guy who manages
the multiplex in Castine City'

519
00:26:59,705 --> 00:27:01,968
he remembers a drunk
couple fighting in the lobby.

520
00:27:02,055 --> 00:27:04,144
The woman was screaming
about the movie being too loud.

521
00:27:04,231 --> 00:27:06,407
Ten o'clock show.
Sound familiar?

522
00:27:06,494 --> 00:27:08,627
Go and show him a picture
of Leslie and Narcisco.

523
00:27:08,714 --> 00:27:11,412
If he IDs them,
that lets them out too.

524
00:27:11,499 --> 00:27:13,936
We're clearing people. We're
supposed to be catching them.

525
00:27:14,023 --> 00:27:15,155
Mmm.

526
00:27:17,287 --> 00:27:18,462
[thud]

527
00:27:19,812 --> 00:27:20,900
[thud]

528
00:27:20,987 --> 00:27:22,249
[thud]

529
00:27:25,513 --> 00:27:27,776
[female #1]
'We've tried everything.'

530
00:27:27,863 --> 00:27:31,084
She finished her fourth
course of chemo last week.

531
00:27:32,955 --> 00:27:36,045
And then the, uh, t-tumors
in her lungs are growing.

532
00:27:37,656 --> 00:27:39,005
Cool shirt.

533
00:27:39,092 --> 00:27:41,572
[chuckles]
Thank you.

534
00:27:41,660 --> 00:27:44,358
[coughing]

535
00:27:44,445 --> 00:27:47,361
[hissing]

536
00:27:49,755 --> 00:27:52,453
[female #1]
'Now the doctors say
there's nothing they can do.'

537
00:27:52,540 --> 00:27:55,499
'Just...make her comfortable.'

538
00:27:55,586 --> 00:28:00,766
I know it...must be difficult.

539
00:28:00,853 --> 00:28:03,203
So when I heard
about the crystal..

540
00:28:03,290 --> 00:28:06,772
Ah, yes. The crystal.

541
00:28:23,005 --> 00:28:25,878
[instrumental music]

542
00:28:27,531 --> 00:28:29,142
Does it really work?

543
00:28:32,406 --> 00:28:33,973
Will it shrink the tumors?

544
00:28:36,236 --> 00:28:37,411
Observe.

545
00:28:38,978 --> 00:28:40,501
Decide for yourself.

546
00:28:42,285 --> 00:28:45,158
[music continues]

547
00:28:48,465 --> 00:28:50,337
- Patrick?
- Ahem.

548
00:28:53,688 --> 00:28:56,604
[music continues]

549
00:29:02,262 --> 00:29:03,437
Son?

550
00:29:05,961 --> 00:29:08,703
[music continues]

551
00:29:09,443 --> 00:29:11,706
I'm sorry.

552
00:29:11,793 --> 00:29:12,968
Patrick.

553
00:29:15,623 --> 00:29:17,756
What's wrong?

554
00:29:17,843 --> 00:29:21,847
Oh, he...it's
a stressful process.

555
00:29:23,152 --> 00:29:25,024
He just needs some air.

556
00:29:26,721 --> 00:29:28,462
Won't be long.

557
00:29:29,855 --> 00:29:30,986
[coughing]

558
00:29:32,466 --> 00:29:34,685
[indistinct chattering]

559
00:29:36,426 --> 00:29:38,602
- Get up and get back in there.
- I can't do it. I can't.

560
00:29:38,689 --> 00:29:42,128
Get up now. What part?

561
00:29:42,215 --> 00:29:45,218
Hmm? What part can't you do?

562
00:29:45,305 --> 00:29:48,395
The gag? That's easy.
I did the hard part.

563
00:29:48,482 --> 00:29:51,354
I put the money in the tent.
All you gotta do is pick it up.

564
00:29:51,441 --> 00:29:53,617
She's dying. Okay?

565
00:29:53,704 --> 00:29:55,968
We're stealing
from a dying girl.

566
00:29:56,055 --> 00:29:59,536
Okay. Yeah, we're all dying,
kid. Okay? We're all dying.

567
00:29:59,623 --> 00:30:00,842
But what we're giving her

568
00:30:00,929 --> 00:30:02,409
because, yeah, she'll
be dead by Tuesday

569
00:30:02,496 --> 00:30:06,065
and needs it more
than most ishope.

570
00:30:06,152 --> 00:30:07,762
Hmm? Do you get that?

571
00:30:07,849 --> 00:30:09,416
I can't do it.

572
00:30:11,766 --> 00:30:12,898
Okay.

573
00:30:14,464 --> 00:30:17,946
You're either with
the show, or you're not.

574
00:30:18,033 --> 00:30:19,730
You're a loser

575
00:30:19,818 --> 00:30:22,690
or you're someone
who plays the losers.

576
00:30:22,777 --> 00:30:24,953
And you can't just back
outwhen you feel like it

577
00:30:25,040 --> 00:30:27,913
when it's morally convenient,
when you don't have the guts.

578
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:29,262
I've never backed out.

579
00:30:29,349 --> 00:30:31,699
I've been carrying
you for a long time.

580
00:30:31,786 --> 00:30:34,093
And it's not gettin'
any easier, son.

581
00:30:34,180 --> 00:30:36,356
No one likes
an aging boy psychic.

582
00:30:36,443 --> 00:30:38,793
Short pants don't look so good
on a kid that needs a shave.

583
00:30:40,882 --> 00:30:42,666
Now.

584
00:30:44,059 --> 00:30:47,454
You're gonna need
a new act. Mm.

585
00:30:47,541 --> 00:30:50,892
'You're gonna work that
out all by yourself?'

586
00:30:50,979 --> 00:30:52,938
'You going solo?'

587
00:30:53,025 --> 00:30:54,417
[laughing]

588
00:30:55,984 --> 00:30:58,160
Yes or no, boy?

589
00:30:58,247 --> 00:31:00,206
Are you with it?
Are you with me?

590
00:31:00,293 --> 00:31:02,425
Right now.
You gotta say. Come on.

591
00:31:10,042 --> 00:31:10,956
[clears throat]

592
00:31:18,659 --> 00:31:19,660
Seven twenty one.

593
00:31:19,747 --> 00:31:21,357
That's the last time we see 'em.

594
00:31:21,444 --> 00:31:23,359
Either one of them could
have gone back to Barney's.

595
00:31:25,057 --> 00:31:26,406
Where you going?

596
00:31:26,493 --> 00:31:28,364
Baseball academy
I was thinking.

597
00:31:28,451 --> 00:31:29,888
Don't we have
to solve this thing?

598
00:31:29,975 --> 00:31:31,106
Rigsby and Van Pelt are talking

599
00:31:31,193 --> 00:31:32,194
to the theater manager now.

600
00:31:32,281 --> 00:31:34,414
The wife? No, no. It wasn't her.

601
00:31:34,501 --> 00:31:35,937
The murder weapon
was a baseball bat.

602
00:31:36,024 --> 00:31:40,899
Baseball bat, baseball
academy, common sense.

603
00:31:40,986 --> 00:31:42,988
- Do you know who the killer is?
- What do you think?

604
00:31:43,075 --> 00:31:44,685
I think you said,
"what do you think?"

605
00:31:44,772 --> 00:31:46,339
to make me think you do
so I'll go with you

606
00:31:46,426 --> 00:31:47,862
'but really you don't.'

607
00:31:47,949 --> 00:31:50,212
[chuckles]
Cho?

608
00:31:50,299 --> 00:31:52,519
Baseball bat, baseball academy,
that's not common sense.

609
00:31:52,606 --> 00:31:54,260
Great. We'll all go.

610
00:31:56,436 --> 00:31:59,265
[instrumental music]

611
00:32:04,183 --> 00:32:05,401
[Freddy]
'Alright, fellas, fellas'

612
00:32:05,488 --> 00:32:06,837
'listen up here
a minute, please.'

613
00:32:06,925 --> 00:32:09,231
Before we start..

614
00:32:09,318 --> 00:32:12,017
...I just wanna say a few
words about Barney Sloop.

615
00:32:13,932 --> 00:32:16,456
He was a great partner..

616
00:32:16,543 --> 00:32:18,371
...a great friend to all of us

617
00:32:18,458 --> 00:32:21,156
and most of all...a great friend

618
00:32:21,243 --> 00:32:23,376
to the game of baseball itself.

619
00:32:23,463 --> 00:32:25,639
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

620
00:32:25,726 --> 00:32:27,946
Let us bow our heads.

621
00:32:32,124 --> 00:32:34,082
Okay then.

622
00:32:34,169 --> 00:32:37,390
That brings us to Snake
Gallidos and Scotty Sinclair.

623
00:32:37,477 --> 00:32:40,219
'Barney's last and maybe
his greatest discoveries.'

624
00:32:40,306 --> 00:32:43,352
Two pitchers with
huge franchise potential.

625
00:32:43,439 --> 00:32:47,443
In a few minutes, guys...
you're gonna see the future.

626
00:32:47,530 --> 00:32:52,187
Meanwhile...grab
some food and a beer..

627
00:32:52,274 --> 00:32:54,668
...and make sure you've
brought your checkbooks.

628
00:32:58,672 --> 00:33:00,891
What are you doing here?

629
00:33:00,979 --> 00:33:03,068
Well, we thought you
might be relieved to know

630
00:33:03,155 --> 00:33:06,941
that we know you're
innocent, so...you can relax.

631
00:33:07,028 --> 00:33:09,422
Go out there and be great.

632
00:33:09,509 --> 00:33:12,077
- 'You're gonna be superstars.'
- That's right, baby.

633
00:33:12,164 --> 00:33:17,386
Women, cars, adulation, buckets
of money all there for you.

634
00:33:17,473 --> 00:33:20,041
So who cares if your dad steals
a little here and there, huh?

635
00:33:22,826 --> 00:33:24,785
- Hey, he didn't steal.
- Really?

636
00:33:26,830 --> 00:33:28,484
Yeah. He just set up
a new bank account.

637
00:33:28,571 --> 00:33:31,226
Oh. Oh.

638
00:33:31,313 --> 00:33:32,532
And that's what Barney told you

639
00:33:32,619 --> 00:33:33,794
when you went
over there to argue

640
00:33:33,881 --> 00:33:35,839
to, uh, accuse him of stealing.

641
00:33:35,926 --> 00:33:38,494
That your dad opened a new
account without telling you.

642
00:33:38,581 --> 00:33:39,887
I don't think you're
helping here, man.

643
00:33:39,974 --> 00:33:43,108
Yes, you two...
you have the gift.

644
00:33:43,195 --> 00:33:46,415
The question is this, what are
you gonna do with that gift?

645
00:33:48,504 --> 00:33:50,158
- Play baseball?
- That's right.

646
00:33:50,245 --> 00:33:51,507
You're gonna play baseball.

647
00:33:51,594 --> 00:33:52,595
You're gonna sell
soap, you're gonna

648
00:33:52,682 --> 00:33:53,944
be part of the big machine.

649
00:33:54,032 --> 00:33:55,294
No, no, no. Not soap, man.

650
00:33:55,381 --> 00:33:59,254
My own cologne.
"Snake. For men."

651
00:33:59,341 --> 00:34:01,735
- That sounds good.
- So we sell ourselves.

652
00:34:01,822 --> 00:34:03,432
I mean, what else
are we gonna do?

653
00:34:03,519 --> 00:34:04,955
Well, I'm just saying be careful

654
00:34:05,043 --> 00:34:08,002
that you sell your
talent and not your soul.

655
00:34:08,089 --> 00:34:10,439
Don't let other people run
your lives, not even your dads.

656
00:34:10,526 --> 00:34:12,659
And trust me, I know
what I'm talking about.

657
00:34:12,746 --> 00:34:13,921
Oh, yeah?

658
00:34:14,008 --> 00:34:15,096
[chuckles]

659
00:34:15,183 --> 00:34:16,793
What's your talent, old man?

660
00:34:16,880 --> 00:34:21,407
Me? Uh..

661
00:34:21,494 --> 00:34:23,148
I read minds, and there's been

662
00:34:23,235 --> 00:34:24,584
plenty of times
that I've misused that.

663
00:34:24,671 --> 00:34:27,500
Read minds, man? Get real.

664
00:34:27,587 --> 00:34:28,936
I am real.

665
00:34:29,023 --> 00:34:31,460
Just like most
people read books

666
00:34:31,547 --> 00:34:33,375
I...read minds.

667
00:34:33,462 --> 00:34:34,985
[snaps fingers]
Okay, what am I thinking?

668
00:34:35,073 --> 00:34:36,683
You're thinking,
"Holy crap, I hope he can't

669
00:34:36,770 --> 00:34:39,947
really read minds. Otherwise I'd
be in deep trouble right now."

670
00:34:40,034 --> 00:34:41,166
Right?

671
00:34:41,253 --> 00:34:43,559
[Snake and Scotty laughing]

672
00:34:43,646 --> 00:34:46,345
Okay. Cho, could you hand
me that pencil, please?

673
00:34:49,696 --> 00:34:51,437
Scotty, concentrate.

674
00:34:51,524 --> 00:34:53,656
Think of your birthday.
Don't tell me.

675
00:34:53,743 --> 00:34:56,485
Month, day, year. Concentrate.

676
00:34:57,791 --> 00:34:59,097
Alright. I'm doing it.

677
00:34:59,184 --> 00:35:00,489
He's messing with us, man.

678
00:35:00,576 --> 00:35:02,404
- 'Come on, we need to go--'
- Shh!

679
00:35:03,666 --> 00:35:05,277
I'm reading his mind.

680
00:35:07,888 --> 00:35:10,804
[instrumental music]

681
00:35:15,809 --> 00:35:18,333
Okay, got it.

682
00:35:18,420 --> 00:35:21,293
[music continues]

683
00:35:24,948 --> 00:35:27,081
What's your birthday, Scotty?

684
00:35:27,168 --> 00:35:30,389
- April 10th, '92.
- "April 10th, '92."

685
00:35:32,304 --> 00:35:35,002
Now how much money you wanna
bet that I can't read minds?

686
00:35:35,089 --> 00:35:37,570
'You're gonna be a big
shot baseball player'

687
00:35:37,657 --> 00:35:39,833
'make a lot of money.'

688
00:35:39,920 --> 00:35:41,922
How much of that money
are you willing to bet

689
00:35:42,009 --> 00:35:43,750
that I can't read minds?

690
00:35:43,837 --> 00:35:44,925
No way.

691
00:35:45,012 --> 00:35:46,883
Snake, you want
in on the action?

692
00:35:46,970 --> 00:35:49,321
Cho's not going near it.
He knows better.

693
00:35:49,408 --> 00:35:51,888
Show it to me.
No way. Come on. Show it.

694
00:35:53,803 --> 00:35:56,632
[music continues]

695
00:35:58,417 --> 00:36:02,203
- Okay, that's sick.
- Maybe he read it somewhere.

696
00:36:02,290 --> 00:36:04,684
Snake, it's my talent.

697
00:36:04,771 --> 00:36:09,341
You want to try? Your birthday.
Just think of it. It's okay.

698
00:36:10,559 --> 00:36:12,213
[chuckles]

699
00:36:12,300 --> 00:36:15,216
I got to warm up, man. Let's go.

700
00:36:15,303 --> 00:36:17,566
Alright. Maybe another time.

701
00:36:17,653 --> 00:36:19,351
- 'Good luck.'
- Thanks.

702
00:36:19,438 --> 00:36:21,396
- 'You too.'
- Thanks.

703
00:36:24,573 --> 00:36:25,531
What was that about?

704
00:36:25,618 --> 00:36:27,315
Just confirming a hunch.

705
00:36:31,972 --> 00:36:33,278
[sighs]

706
00:36:38,065 --> 00:36:40,241
- You okay?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

707
00:36:40,328 --> 00:36:43,026
Just give me a minute,
I'll close this thing.

708
00:36:43,113 --> 00:36:45,942
- My dad hated baseball.
- You gotta get over that.

709
00:36:46,029 --> 00:36:48,118
Probably never would have
made the big leagues anyway.

710
00:36:56,214 --> 00:36:59,260
This crystal
is from ancient Egypt.

711
00:36:59,347 --> 00:37:02,785
'Its healing powers
are legendary.'

712
00:37:02,872 --> 00:37:06,441
'Where there is sickness...
it brings health.'

713
00:37:08,443 --> 00:37:10,402
This may be hard to watch.

714
00:37:12,752 --> 00:37:13,709
No. Don't.

715
00:37:13,796 --> 00:37:15,450
[coughing]

716
00:37:20,020 --> 00:37:21,978
And when the crystal
is applied..

717
00:37:23,980 --> 00:37:25,939
'...the burn is healed.'

718
00:37:26,983 --> 00:37:29,682
[instrumental music]

719
00:37:31,336 --> 00:37:34,121
The same thing
happens with the tumors.

720
00:37:34,208 --> 00:37:37,429
- They just disappear.
- I want it.

721
00:37:37,516 --> 00:37:40,083
Ma'am, we are here
for the next three days.

722
00:37:40,170 --> 00:37:41,694
You can have as many
appointments as you like.

723
00:37:41,781 --> 00:37:43,913
No!

724
00:37:44,000 --> 00:37:47,482
I want the crystal.
I want to buy it.

725
00:37:47,569 --> 00:37:50,137
Oh, that's not possible, ma'am.

726
00:37:50,224 --> 00:37:53,532
- I brought cash.
- Ma'am, I'm sorry.

727
00:37:53,619 --> 00:37:56,230
It's been in our family
for the past six generations.

728
00:37:56,317 --> 00:37:59,059
- 'I can't.'
- Please.

729
00:37:59,146 --> 00:38:00,626
I'm truly sorry, ma'am.

730
00:38:00,713 --> 00:38:03,193
Dad...she needs it.

731
00:38:08,851 --> 00:38:11,158
Just give it to her!

732
00:38:11,245 --> 00:38:12,420
Please!

733
00:38:14,292 --> 00:38:16,250
I'm begging you.

734
00:38:22,909 --> 00:38:26,129
[laughing]
Ten grand, my son.

735
00:38:26,216 --> 00:38:27,914
You were great in there.

736
00:38:28,001 --> 00:38:30,525
The crying, oh,
that was fantastic.

737
00:38:30,612 --> 00:38:32,484
I almost bought it myself.

738
00:38:35,356 --> 00:38:38,316
You earned this. Every penny.

739
00:38:41,493 --> 00:38:43,364
I'm gonna be
a little late tonight.

740
00:38:43,451 --> 00:38:45,540
'The sideshow boys got
a little poker going.'

741
00:38:45,627 --> 00:38:48,761
So, uh...wish me luck, hmm?

742
00:38:51,894 --> 00:38:54,288
[instrumental music]

743
00:38:55,333 --> 00:38:57,857
[bell ringing]

744
00:39:05,952 --> 00:39:09,434
Snake, you left before
I got to read your mind.

745
00:39:09,521 --> 00:39:11,827
What are you talking about?
Go away now. We got to focus.

746
00:39:11,914 --> 00:39:13,742
Oh, I was just trying
to get his date of birth.

747
00:39:13,829 --> 00:39:17,006
March 5th,'92. Okay? You happy?

748
00:39:18,181 --> 00:39:20,619
March 5th,'92. That's weird.

749
00:39:20,706 --> 00:39:24,753
I got the March 5th bit right,
but I got the, uh, year wrong.

750
00:39:24,840 --> 00:39:27,756
Never off by that much.
Mmm, five years.

751
00:39:29,236 --> 00:39:30,411
What are you doing?

752
00:39:30,498 --> 00:39:33,545
That would make you
22, 22 years old.

753
00:39:33,632 --> 00:39:34,981
Get out of here.

754
00:39:35,068 --> 00:39:36,809
That's the same age as
your brother, uh, Carlos.

755
00:39:36,896 --> 00:39:38,419
- That's his name, isn't it?
- Shut your mouth, man!

756
00:39:38,506 --> 00:39:40,856
- Get outta here!
- Take it easy.

757
00:39:40,943 --> 00:39:43,468
Barney found out,
didn't he? Yeah?

758
00:39:43,555 --> 00:39:46,819
He found out that Snake was 22.
He was gonna send him home.

759
00:39:46,906 --> 00:39:48,124
[whispering]
Shut your mouth, man.

760
00:39:48,211 --> 00:39:49,778
What the hell's going on here?

761
00:39:49,865 --> 00:39:53,521
Jupiter killed Barney
to conceal Snake's real age.

762
00:39:53,608 --> 00:39:55,654
Holy crap. Is this true?

763
00:39:58,352 --> 00:40:01,747
[Jupiter]
I tried to reason with him,
but he just walked away.

764
00:40:01,834 --> 00:40:03,009
[thud]

765
00:40:07,709 --> 00:40:09,276
- Papa?
- Don't say a word, Snake.

766
00:40:09,363 --> 00:40:12,714
No digas nada.
He doesn't know nothing.

767
00:40:12,801 --> 00:40:16,196
- Nothing about what?
- Holy crap.

768
00:40:16,283 --> 00:40:18,546
I...I didn't do nothing.
I'm not saying nothing.

769
00:40:18,633 --> 00:40:20,200
Oh, Jupiter, come on.
Let's be honest here.

770
00:40:20,287 --> 00:40:23,638
We'll let your kid throw.
Right, Mr. Fitch? Yeah?

771
00:40:25,858 --> 00:40:28,687
How old are you really,
kid? On the bible.

772
00:40:32,212 --> 00:40:33,822
Twenty two.

773
00:40:33,909 --> 00:40:36,172
Then you might have a shot.

774
00:40:36,259 --> 00:40:37,957
Middle reliever maybe.

775
00:40:39,828 --> 00:40:42,440
Double my cut, he can throw.

776
00:40:44,659 --> 00:40:46,052
Deal.

777
00:40:46,139 --> 00:40:48,054
Put your hands behind your back.

778
00:40:48,141 --> 00:40:50,012
You're under arrest for
the murder of Barney Sloop.

779
00:40:53,581 --> 00:40:55,931
- Dad.
- Man up, kid.

780
00:40:56,018 --> 00:40:57,933
Remember to keep the ball low.

781
00:40:58,020 --> 00:40:59,065
You get in trouble,
throw 'em the slider.

782
00:40:59,152 --> 00:41:00,501
[Cho]
Come on.

783
00:41:00,588 --> 00:41:03,461
[instrumental music]

784
00:41:08,509 --> 00:41:10,555
I just feel a little bit dizzy.

785
00:41:13,122 --> 00:41:16,299
I'm just gonna take a knee.

786
00:41:16,386 --> 00:41:17,475
I'm good.

787
00:41:19,389 --> 00:41:20,782
[male #3]
'Come on!'

788
00:41:25,047 --> 00:41:26,701
[male #7]
'Strike three. You're out.'

789
00:41:26,788 --> 00:41:30,792
- 'Nice pitch.'
- Yes! Ha ha.

790
00:41:30,879 --> 00:41:33,012
- Oh, you got lucky on that one.
- I-I struck him out.

791
00:41:33,099 --> 00:41:35,101
You set him up with the heater.

792
00:41:35,188 --> 00:41:38,452
You don't use it for an out,
not in that situation.

793
00:41:38,539 --> 00:41:39,758
I struck him out.

794
00:41:39,845 --> 00:41:41,890
We'll talk about this later.

795
00:41:44,197 --> 00:41:47,287
- I'm gonna make our deal.
- No. You won't.

796
00:41:48,941 --> 00:41:50,856
I hired an agent.

797
00:41:50,943 --> 00:41:53,685
[instrumental music]

798
00:42:02,128 --> 00:42:04,043
Let's go see a doctor.

799
00:42:04,130 --> 00:42:07,655
- Why? Are you feeling unwell?
- No, you are.

800
00:42:07,742 --> 00:42:11,006
- Cho said you almost fainted.
- Oh, I was just pretending.

801
00:42:11,093 --> 00:42:13,574
I hate these kind
of dramatic scenes. Poor kid.

802
00:42:13,661 --> 00:42:15,576
Liar. You just don't
wanna go to the doctor.

803
00:42:15,663 --> 00:42:17,012
Well, what's
a doctor gonna say?

804
00:42:17,099 --> 00:42:19,145
"You banged your head.
Be careful."

805
00:42:19,232 --> 00:42:20,973
- You might need an MRI.
- Oh.

806
00:42:21,060 --> 00:42:22,975
Now you're really
selling it. Sounds great.

807
00:42:24,759 --> 00:42:27,022
Are you okay?

808
00:42:27,109 --> 00:42:28,633
Just kidding.

809
00:42:28,720 --> 00:42:31,592
[instrumental music]

810
00:42:34,247 --> 00:42:36,423
[male narrator]
Stay tuned for scenes
from our next episode.

811
00:42:39,948 --> 00:42:42,081
[theme music]

